# Sheet

A side panel sliding flush to the screen edge — same native
`<dialog>` as the dialog, positioned. The header's notification
drawer is a sheet.

## When to use

- Supplementary content consulted while keeping the page in context:
  notification lists, record peeks, filter panels.

## When not to use

- Blocking decisions — `dialog` (see the *Overlays* pattern page
  decision table).
- A form home: fields plus a save button have outgrown a sheet —
  give the flow a page.
- Primary navigation — that is the `sidebar`, which is part of the
  shell, not an overlay.

## Usage

`render_sheet` (`Gesso::Components::SheetHelper`) validates the `side` and
renders the positioned `<dialog>` shell — nothing else. **The heading
and close control are not part of the shell; you supply them in the
block** (this is why the previews below show a title and an `x` button
even though the component itself ships neither). Render the sheet inside
a `[data-controller="drawer"]` element alongside the trigger that opens
it.

| Param | Default | Notes |
| ----- | ------- | ----- |
| `id` | required | targeted by the trigger |
| `aria_label` | required | accessible name for the panel |
| `side` | `"right"` | see **Sides** below |
| `classes` | — | extra classes on the `<dialog>` |

## Sides

### Right (default)

The standard side panel — details, record peeks, filter panels.

```erb
<%%= tag.div data: { controller: "drawer" } do %>
  <%%= button_tag "Open sheet", class: "btn",
        data: { action: "click->drawer#open" } %>

  <%%= render_sheet(id: "demo-sheet", aria_label: "Demo sheet") do %>
    <%%= tag.div class: "flex flex-col h-full" do %>
      <%%= tag.div class: "flex items-center justify-between px-6 py-4 border-b" do %>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">Sheet title</h2>

        <%%= button_tag aria: { label: "Close sheet" }, class: "btn-icon-ghost",
              data: { action: "click->drawer#close" } do %>
          <%%= inline_svg_tag "icons/x.svg", class: "size-5" %>
        <%% end %>
      <%% end %>

      <%%= tag.div class: "flex-1 overflow-y-auto px-6 py-4" do %>
        Sheet body content.
      <%% end %>
    <%% end %>
  <%% end %>
<%% end %>
```

<%= embed :sheet, :default %>

### Left

When the panel relates to the sidebar's content, anchored to the same
edge. Identical to the above — pass `side: "left"`:

```erb
<%%= render_sheet(id: "menu", aria_label: "Menu", side: "left") do %>
  <!-- same panel chrome: heading, close control, body -->
<%% end %>
```

<%= embed :sheet, :left %>

## Do and don't

- Do give the sheet's content its own visible heading and close
  control — the shell deliberately ships neither.
- Do default to `side: "right"`; `left` is for panels that relate
  to the sidebar's content.
- Don't let a sheet hold unsaved input that dismissal would strand —
  dismissal is one Escape away by design (see *Overlays*).
- Don't open a sheet from a sheet; close the first.

## Accessibility and content

- Native `<dialog>` via `showModal()`: focus trap, Escape and
  backdrop dismissal as the dialog — the positioning is only CSS
  (`sheet.css`).
- `aria_label` is required because the shell has no built-in title —
  name the panel ("Notifications"), not the mechanism ("Side
  panel").
